00:24:37.042 --> 00:24:38.677 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, every day
there are new headlines

00:24:38.677 --> 00:24:43.215 align:start size:84% position:16%
about, you know,
meat producing fields

00:24:43.215 --> 00:24:45.183 align:start size:88% position:13%
and all of these things
that are on fire.

00:24:45.183 --> 00:24:47.319
Factories seem to be burning up,

00:24:47.319 --> 00:24:49.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
that our food security
really seems to be

00:24:49.955 --> 00:24:51.156
threatened right now.

00:24:51.156 --> 00:24:53.091 align:start size:84% position:16%
There was this weird
thing in Kansas

00:24:53.091 --> 00:24:57.028
with 2000 cattle dying out of
nowhere, supposedly from heat.

00:24:57.028 --> 00:24:58.663
What is going on here?

00:25:00.031 --> 00:25:01.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Well, I've been talking
about food security

00:25:01.466 --> 00:25:04.569 align:start size:84% position:16%
as a national security
issue for 15 years.

00:25:04.569 --> 00:25:07.172 align:start size:88% position:13%
I served on a
committee in the state.

00:25:07.172 --> 00:25:08.673 align:start size:84% position:16%
Of course I am a
farmer and a rancher.

00:25:08.673 --> 00:25:10.375
That's how I've made my
living my entire life,

00:25:10.375 --> 00:25:12.811
until I got involved in
government and politics.

00:25:12.811 --> 00:25:14.980
But beyond that, I
served on a committee

00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:17.616
that oversaw the federal
farm programs in the state.

00:25:17.616 --> 00:25:21.786 align:start size:97% position:3%
But I recognized that
America has always embraced

00:25:21.786 --> 00:25:26.491
a food policy of having it be
diversified in the country.

00:25:26.491 --> 00:25:29.094
So that one person doesn't
control our food supply,

00:25:29.094 --> 00:25:32.430 align:start size:97% position:3%
that many different farmers
and small businesses do

00:25:32.430 --> 00:25:35.433
and processors, but
that also we have had

00:25:35.433 --> 00:25:37.002
a cheap food policy.

00:25:37.002 --> 00:25:39.004
We wanted every single
family in this country

00:25:39.004 --> 00:25:40.705
to be able to afford to put food

00:25:40.705 --> 00:25:42.307
on the table for their families.

00:25:42.307 --> 00:25:46.144 align:start position:0%
And I've been drawing attention
for 15 years to the fact

00:25:46.144 --> 00:25:49.781
that we are losing both of
those battles that we have.

00:25:49.781 --> 00:25:51.883 align:start size:84% position:16%
We have more and more
foreign countries

00:25:51.883 --> 00:25:54.319 align:start size:84% position:16%
buying up our
processing systems.

00:25:54.319 --> 00:25:56.121
They're buying up our
fertilizer companies,

00:25:56.121 --> 00:25:59.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
our chemical companies,
our processing facilities,

00:25:59.624 --> 00:26:02.060 align:start size:97% position:3%
not only is China
manipulating their currency,

00:26:02.060 --> 00:26:04.429 align:start size:97% position:3%
but stealing our IP,
building up their military.

00:26:04.429 --> 00:26:06.264
They're also buying our land.

00:26:06.264 --> 00:26:09.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
They own a lot of our
food supply chain system.

00:26:09.701 --> 00:26:12.170 align:start size:88% position:13%
And when another country
controls our food,

00:26:12.170 --> 00:26:14.372
that is when they control us.

00:26:14.372 --> 00:26:15.941
So they're not dummies.

00:26:15.941 --> 00:26:18.577
And I think that
these higher costs

00:26:18.577 --> 00:26:20.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
are already forcing
families to make decisions

00:26:20.812 --> 00:26:23.815
on what they can buy and what
they can feed their families.

00:26:23.815 --> 00:26:26.384 align:start position:0%
And when we get another
country that truly does control

00:26:26.384 --> 00:26:29.955 align:start position:0%
the entire supply system,
that's when America gets scary.

00:26:29.955 --> 00:26:33.124
You know, I think a
virus was a situation

00:26:33.124 --> 00:26:36.227 align:start size:84% position:16%
where the entire
country was nervous.

00:26:36.227 --> 00:26:38.830 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would say, wait
till there's no food

00:26:38.830 --> 00:26:40.131
on the grocery store shelves.

00:26:40.131 --> 00:26:41.633 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's really
when you start to see

00:26:41.633 --> 00:26:43.802 align:start size:84% position:16%
our way of life
being threatened. So.

00:26:43.802 --> 00:26:45.236
- So, so what do we
do? What do we do?

00:26:45.236 --> 00:26:47.238 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, Biden said it
himself a couple months ago,

00:26:47.238 --> 00:26:49.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
food shortages, you know,
I think what was it,

00:26:49.941 --> 00:26:52.243
the Economist or one
of the major magazines,

00:26:52.243 --> 00:26:54.312
the food shortages are coming.

00:26:54.312 --> 00:26:56.982
World economic forum worrying
about it, talking about it.

00:26:56.982 --> 00:27:00.085
Bill Gates is now the
largest farm land owner

00:27:00.085 --> 00:27:01.319
in the United States.

00:27:01.319 --> 00:27:03.254
I mean, what do you do
as a governor of state?

00:27:03.254 --> 00:27:04.723
What do you do?

00:27:04.723 --> 00:27:06.491
- Well, first of all, I have
to be honest and talk about it.

00:27:06.491 --> 00:27:09.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
This administration's
not talking about
solving the problem.

00:27:09.527 --> 00:27:12.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
And in fact, they're
facilitating foreign countries

00:27:12.998 --> 00:27:15.834
coming in and buying up
our systems and our land.

00:27:15.834 --> 00:27:17.535 align:start size:84% position:16%
So the administration
being honest

00:27:17.535 --> 00:27:20.071
and recognizing it,
is a real challenge.

00:27:20.071 --> 00:27:21.539 align:start size:84% position:16%
In solving it
would be important.

00:27:21.539 --> 00:27:25.043
Cutting regulations to allow
more of our American businesses

00:27:25.043 --> 00:27:27.045
to buy back these facilities,

00:27:27.045 --> 00:27:28.580
to be in production agriculture,

00:27:28.580 --> 00:27:30.081 align:start size:81% position:19%
to grow our own
food is important.

00:27:30.081 --> 00:27:32.817
Right now they're attacking
our farmers and ranchers.

00:27:32.817 --> 00:27:35.820
And they're penalizing them
and putting heavy regulations

00:27:35.820 --> 00:27:38.590 align:start size:97% position:3%
on them that don't allow
people to work on their land.

00:27:38.590 --> 00:27:40.225 align:start size:88% position:13%
Don't allow their
children to participate

00:27:40.225 --> 00:27:41.593
in the business at all.

00:27:41.593 --> 00:27:43.094
And in South Dakota here,

00:27:43.094 --> 00:27:45.296
we've been aggressive in
cutting back regulations.

00:27:45.296 --> 00:27:47.499 align:start size:84% position:16%
We've also been
aggressive in building

00:27:47.499 --> 00:27:48.900
our own processing plants.

00:27:48.900 --> 00:27:51.002 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've given millions
and millions of grants

00:27:51.002 --> 00:27:53.471 align:start size:97% position:3%
to people who want to
build a meat packing plant,

00:27:53.471 --> 00:27:56.775
or expand a facility that
would put value added food

00:27:56.775 --> 00:27:58.209
on the table for families here,

00:27:58.209 --> 00:28:00.045
so that we control
our own destiny.

00:28:00.045 --> 00:28:02.914 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that many, many of
these producers can control

00:28:02.914 --> 00:28:06.084 align:start size:97% position:3%
their own supply chain to
get it right to the customer.

00:28:06.084 --> 00:28:10.655 align:start size:97% position:3%
We're bypassing a lot of these
big corporations that own

00:28:10.655 --> 00:28:13.491 align:start size:97% position:3%
the systems, that are
stealing the profits away from

00:28:13.491 --> 00:28:15.126 align:start size:88% position:13%
those that are actually
growing the food

00:28:15.126 --> 00:28:17.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
and making sure we're
putting that control back

00:28:17.462 --> 00:28:18.797
in the hands of the consumer,

00:28:18.797 --> 00:28:21.266
who needs to put that
food on the table.

00:28:21.266 --> 00:28:23.334
- What do you make of this
administration when it comes

00:28:23.334 --> 00:28:24.536
to everything we've
talked about here?

00:28:24.536 --> 00:28:26.604 align:start size:84% position:16%
Do you believe that
it's ineptitude

00:28:26.604 --> 00:28:28.973
or do you think that
this is intentional?

00:28:28.973 --> 00:28:31.543 align:start size:84% position:16%
Everything that's
happening right now?

00:28:31.543 --> 00:28:35.246
- Well, you know, there's
been a year and a half here

00:28:35.246 --> 00:28:37.182
where I thought, you
know, this guy's like

00:28:37.182 --> 00:28:39.150 align:start size:84% position:16%
the George Castanza
of government.

00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:42.520
Like his, every instinct
he makes is just wrong.

00:28:42.520 --> 00:28:43.922
- Right, he should be
making the reverse.

00:28:43.922 --> 00:28:44.956
- If he would wake
up in the morning.

00:28:44.956 --> 00:28:45.890
Yes, he should.

