00:38:21.699 --> 00:38:25.002
And I was passionate about
this constitutional right.

00:38:25.002 --> 00:38:27.271 align:start size:88% position:13%
So we had a big
ceremony in the rotunda

00:38:27.271 --> 00:38:29.607 align:start size:88% position:13%
and celebrated this bill
finally becoming law

00:38:29.607 --> 00:38:31.275
in the state of South Dakota.

00:38:31.275 --> 00:38:34.078
And since then we've passed
quite a few different bills

00:38:34.078 --> 00:38:37.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
and pieces of legislation
that make it clear

00:38:37.214 --> 00:38:39.317
that if you wanna exercise
your second amendment rights

00:38:39.317 --> 00:38:41.619
in South Dakota, please do.

00:38:41.619 --> 00:38:44.989 align:start size:88% position:13%
In fact, this last
year I removed all fees

00:38:44.989 --> 00:38:47.024
for concealed carry permits.

00:38:47.024 --> 00:38:48.893 align:start size:81% position:19%
Any permit that
would be required.

00:38:48.893 --> 00:38:51.095 align:start size:97% position:3%
And said the state of
South Dakota would even pay

00:38:51.095 --> 00:38:53.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
for a person's federal
background check.

00:38:53.964 --> 00:38:55.533
So there would be zero cost

00:38:55.533 --> 00:38:57.902
to exercising your second
amendment rights here.

00:38:57.902 --> 00:39:00.237 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think it's important
we lead by example

00:39:00.237 --> 00:39:03.107
and the discussion on
violence and tragedies

00:39:03.107 --> 00:39:08.045 align:start size:97% position:3%
that happens in this country
is heartbreaking to see.

00:39:08.045 --> 00:39:10.581
I think what we need
to remember though,

00:39:10.581 --> 00:39:13.751
is that this is a
constitutionally
protected right.

00:39:13.751 --> 00:39:15.553 align:start size:81% position:19%
And it is a right,
that guarantees

00:39:15.553 --> 00:39:18.456
all the other Bill of Rights.

00:39:19.757 --> 00:39:23.060
It is the militia,
the citizen militia,

00:39:23.060 --> 00:39:25.930 align:start size:88% position:13%
that fought for our
freedom in this country

00:39:25.930 --> 00:39:29.200
during the Revolutionary War
did so with their own weapons.

00:39:29.200 --> 00:39:32.069
With the weapons that they
had to feed their families,

00:39:32.069 --> 00:39:33.604
to hunt deer and squirrel.

00:39:33.604 --> 00:39:36.273 align:start size:88% position:13%
They used those to
fight for their freedom

00:39:36.273 --> 00:39:39.844 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they wanted it enshrined
in our Bill of Rights

00:39:39.844 --> 00:39:42.480 align:start position:0%
that we always have the
opportunity for each individual

00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:44.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
in this country to be
able to defend themselves

00:39:44.949 --> 00:39:46.450
with their own weapons.

00:39:46.450 --> 00:39:48.552
And it wasn't from other
people in their community.

00:39:48.552 --> 00:39:50.421 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was from a
corrupt government.

00:39:50.421 --> 00:39:53.124
And that is what I
think is imperative

00:39:53.124 --> 00:39:55.693 align:start size:84% position:16%
is that we remain
focused on the reason

00:39:55.693 --> 00:39:59.230 align:start size:97% position:3%
that the second amendment
exists, talk about the history

00:39:59.230 --> 00:40:02.266
and ensure that we keep
that protection in place.

00:40:02.266 --> 00:40:04.902 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It is unclear to me whether
the government is inept,

00:40:04.902 --> 00:40:07.238
corrupt or malicious
at this point, but,

00:40:07.238 --> 00:40:08.706
- I would say all of the above.

00:40:08.706 --> 00:40:11.008 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It might, it
might be all three.

00:40:11.008 --> 00:40:13.277 align:start size:88% position:13%
And of course, governor,
I cannot let you go

00:40:13.277 --> 00:40:15.613 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
without asking the most
important question.

00:40:15.613 --> 00:40:20.084 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
You knew it was coming,
are you're running in 2024?

00:40:20.084 --> 00:40:21.852
Come on. No, evasive answers.

00:40:21.852 --> 00:40:22.953
- I thought you were asking

00:40:22.953 --> 00:40:24.188 align:start size:88% position:13%
what I had for
breakfast this morning.

00:40:24.188 --> 00:40:27.458
So, you know, I
have no plans to.

00:40:27.458 --> 00:40:30.094 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm running for
reelection this year

00:40:30.094 --> 00:40:33.030
and I have to ask the
people of South Dakota,

00:40:33.030 --> 00:40:35.232
if they'll trust me
to work with them

00:40:35.232 --> 00:40:36.300
for the next four years.

00:40:36.300 --> 00:40:37.935
I'm hopeful they will.

00:40:37.935 --> 00:40:42.573 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I also think 2024,
there'll be a lot of people

00:40:42.573 --> 00:40:44.175 align:start size:84% position:16%
running for president
at that point.

00:40:44.175 --> 00:40:46.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think anybody who wants
to run for president,

00:40:46.277 --> 00:40:47.912
that gets up every single day

00:40:47.912 --> 00:40:49.980
and that's their
number one desire.

00:40:49.980 --> 00:40:52.950
Maybe that's not the kind
of president that we want.

00:40:52.950 --> 00:40:55.119
It might be time for this
country to have someone

00:40:55.119 --> 00:40:57.188 align:start size:84% position:16%
who steps up because
they feel a duty

00:40:57.188 --> 00:40:59.623 align:start size:88% position:13%
to protect this country
and our freedom.

00:41:00.791 --> 00:41:02.026
- Amen.

00:41:02.026 --> 00:41:04.595
Governor Kristi Noem,
thank you very much.

00:41:04.595 --> 00:41:06.897 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Great to visit
with you. Thank you.

